ally began to promote the hotel as a  place of rest and recuperation as well  they built all sorts of new facilities  around the hotel bath facilities steam  cave facilities all sorts of additional  facilities there and in that third hotel  the guests would come and they would be  drawn by the water because they still  advertised the water here they said you  know come to Arrowhead Springs and be  healed by the water there's all these  different types of water here that are  very health inducing for you so come  here and be healed by the water and it  really drew a lot of folks to that third  hotel and finally after so many folks  would come to the to the hotel and say  we really would like to take some of  this water home so the hotel would  package it up for him and send it home  for them to their to their relatives and  so forth and in the other states in the  eastern states and finally somebody got  the bright idea you know this would  probably be a good product to bottle  commercially in in large quantity since  it was so available and was so popular  so in 1909 the first real major bottling  facility came to be here at Arrowhead  Springs the third hotel that was built  in 1905 really began to catch on with  the Hollywood movie stars because  Hollywood was just evolving at that time  the motion picture NIT picture industry  was really just taking hold in Hollywood  in the early 1900s they had found  Southern California because of the great  weather and and year-round filming  ability of the location and all the  geography so the film industry was  really starting to take hold in around  1905 1910 that type of timeframe and so  the folks that were there  in Hollywood wanted a place that they  could that they could get away from town  and they found Arrowhead Springs that  you know it was built in 1905 so it was  a brand new facility it was beautiful  luxurious hotel and it was just far  enough out of town just far enough away  from Hollywood it was about a two-h